{================================================================================
 Script Name : _Backtest_Adaptive_Farmer_v14_PureLong
 MC Load Name: STRATEGY_WILLY_LONG_C
 Description : Matrix Range Capture (Full-Range Consolidation Long)
 Version     : v19.0 (2026-09-27 research build: defaults = live version; new OFF-by-default switches Target_Mode / Min_Gap_Hrs / Size_Mode) (Data4 = Weekly required) (v14.1 base + SetStopContract + SL_Pct 0.55% + Opening Block + Min R:R)
 Symbol      : TXF1 (Taiwan Stock Index Futures Front Month)
 Platform    : MultiCharts 9.0 PowerLanguage x64
 Timeframe   : Data1 = 15M / Data2 = 60M / Data3 = Daily

 ARCHITECTURE REDESIGN (v14.0, 2026-07-03):
   Problem: v13 half-box design splits the box into Bot->Mid and Mid->Top,
            structurally capping reward ratio at ~1.1x. CL_Entry_Bot was a
            dead leg (26 trades, -10.4K). 94% of profit came from
            CL_Entry_Mid targeting only half the box range.

   Solution: Multi-dimensional matrix architecture.
     Dim 1 [Box Qualification]: skip boxes < Min_Box_ATR * ATR (friction filter)
     Dim 2 [Support Zone]:     unified entry at bottom Entry_Zone_Pct of box
     Dim 3 [Dynamic Target]:   Frozen swing high (15M lookback, capped at Box_Top)
     Dim 4 [Trend + Daily]:    unchanged filters from v13

   Pre-verify: Python 28y TWII daily confirmed direction:
     Full-range PF 1.086 vs half-box PF 0.806 (+35%)
     Reward ratio 1.92x vs 0.90x (+113%)
     Filtered variant (large boxes) best: Sharpe +0.366 vs baseline

   Changes from v13.4:
     - REMOVED: CL_Entry_Bot / CL_Entry_Mid dual-leg split
     - REMOVED: v_Leg_IsBot / v_Work_IsBot leg classification
     - REMOVED: CL_TP_Bot / CL_TP_Mid dual-leg targets
     - ADDED:   CL_Entry (unified support zone entry)
     - ADDED:   CL_TP (full-range target = dynamic swing high)
     - ADDED:   Entry_Zone_Pct input (support zone = bottom 50% of box)
     - ADDED:   Min_Box_ATR input (box must be >= N * ATR to trade)
     - ADDED:   Swing_Lookback input (15M bars for dynamic target)
     - KEPT:    All safety modules (Holiday v3, Settlement, ImmediateStop,
                FrozenSL, BreakExit, Registry fail-safe, Manual Kill)
     - KEPT:    BE mechanism code (disabled, BE_Trigger_Pts=0)

 V15.0 CHANGES (2026-07-25, stop loss hardening):
   BUG-1 FIX: Added SetStopContract declaration.
     Without it, 2-lot deployment halves the per-contract stop distance.
     SetStopContract makes SetStopLoss amount per-CONTRACT (lot-invariant).
   BUG-2 FIX: Added SL_Pct percentage-based stop distance cap.
     ATR buffer scales non-linearly with index level. At high ATR, a single
     stop can exceed any reasonable per-trade risk budget. SL_Pct caps the
     maximum stop distance as a percentage of entry price.
     Frozen SL becomes dual-layer: MaxList(ATR_leg, Pct_leg) = tightest.
     SetStopLoss mirrors: MinList(ATR_distance, Pct_distance) = tightest.
     SL_Pct = 0 disables the percentage leg (v14.1 compatible mode).
   BUG-3 FIX: SetStopLoss distance formula unchanged (Close-based proxy).
     Entry via Stop at Box_Btm fills near Close when Close > Box_Btm.
     Close-based distance is a conservative approximation. Combined with
     SL_Pct cap, the engine stop is always a valid safety net.
   FILTER: Opening volatility block (08:45-09:45, Open_Block_End=945).
     Day-session open entries are structurally toxic for consolidation strategies:
     institutions probe/hunt box bottoms at open, invalidating support logic.
     OB930 first pass removed 08:45-09:30 but cascade pushed 19T to 09:45
     (WR 10.5%, -604K). OB945 eliminates cascade; 10:xx is the first
     profitable slot (WR 41%, +134K). Blocks entry SIGNALS whose fills
     would land in the forbidden zone: Time=500 (night session last bar
     -> 09:00 fill) and Time 900..930 (-> 09:15..09:45 fills).
   FILTER: Minimum R:R gate (Min_RR=1.0, requires SL_Pct > 0).
     Rejects entries where Box_Range < Min_RR * Box_Bottom * SL_Pct/100.
     27% of CL_TP trades had R:R < 1.0 (reward < risk). Box width varies
     36-1188 pts but SL_Pct cap is nearly fixed, so narrow boxes create
     structurally negative expected value entries. Optimizable parameter.

 PERFORMANCE (V15.0 w/ OB945, MC9 2026/07/25, 2-lot 2M capital, 1000 slip):
   Net Profit    : 2,446,000 TWD
   Profit Factor : 1.255
   Max Drawdown  : -810,800 (29.4%)
   Win Rate      : 46.3%
   Total Trades  : 376
   Day PF 1.03 / Night PF 1.32

 PERFORMANCE (v14.1 OPTIMIZED, MC9 Excel 2026/07/04, Initial Capital 1M):
   Net Profit    : 2,048,000 TWD (+194% vs v13.4)
   Profit Factor : 1.470 (+24% vs v13.4 1.187)
   Win Rate      : 56.0%
   Reward Ratio  : 1.154
   MDD           : -378,600 (-22.3%)
   Net/MDD       : 5.41
   Total Trades  : 332
   Annual Return : 33.3%
   Sharpe        : 0.302
   Backtest      : 2020/05/12 - 2026/07/04

 OPTIMIZATION (2026-07-04, 2-round MC9 sweep):
   Round 1: range 0.15-0.50 / 1.5-6.0 / 16-64 -> all hit upper bound
   Round 2: expanded 0.15-0.70 / 1.5-10.0 / 16-128 -> converged interior
   Entry_Zone_Pct : 0.30 -> 0.50 (71% of range, plateau confirmed)
   Min_Box_ATR    : 3.0  -> 8.5  (85% of range, off boundary)
   Swing_Lookback : 32   -> 80   (63% of range, plateau confirmed)
================================================================================}

inputs:
    { --- Data2 (60M) Box Detection --- }
    Lookback_Bars(16),
    Range_Shrink_Rate(0.1),
    MA_Len(12),

    { --- R2 (2026-09-24): consolidation first, then box --- }
    Box_New_On(false),          { v18: MUST be false. true = the abandoned v16 "4-hour
                                  consolidation-first" box, which produced 4-7 trades in six
                                  years. The v18 numbers were all measured with the ORIGINAL
                                  box detection, i.e. this switch OFF. }
    Consol_Bars_15M(16),        { 15M bars of the observation window. 16 = 4 hours }
    Consol_Drift_Pct(30),       { net move of the window must be <= N% of window range }
    Box_Touch_Min(2),           { inert while Box_New_On = false }
    Box_Touch_Tol_Pct(4),       { touch tolerance = N% of box width }
    Box_NoWick(true),           { drop an edge made by a single bar wick; use 2nd extreme }

    { --- R2 (2026-09-24 final): risk first, then reward ---
      entry  = box bottom
      stop   = entry - entry * Risk_Pct / 100
      target = entry + RR * stop distance
      RR     = RR_Base * (recent daily range % / one-year median daily range %)
               clamped to [RR_Min, RR_Max]
      A box is traded only when its width >= RR * Risk_Pct (else skipped).
      Box width no longer sets the stop; it only decides go / no-go. }
    { --- v18 (2026-09-26): loss-reduction package ---
      Night_Only   : no entries during the 09:00-13:45 day session.
                     2026-09-27 CORRECTION: the PF 0.78 day figure came from the
                     Python replica (119 day trades). The MC live-version report
                     has 55 day trades before 2026-06-17 averaging +6,909 vs
                     +7,611 at night, and the sign flips year to year (2024 day
                     +312,800 / night -705,600). MC does NOT support this switch.
                     Default OFF until an MC run with interactions says otherwise.
      Stop_Day_Pct : stop distance = previous day's range % x N%.
                     WHY relative: the fixed 0.55% stop is 44 pts at index
                     8,000 and 264 pts at 48,000 - the same input, 6x the
                     real tightness. That is the backtest / live divergence.
                     N=28 is the MC-VALIDATED value (450 trades, net
                     +3,075,200, max DD -698,000, 2026-09-26 report).
                     Do NOT re-tune this digit: the k axis is a spike field,
                     not a plateau (k .26=+2849 .38=+1409 .46=+3302 net pts),
                     so the number itself is noise. What is robust is that
                     EVERY k from 0.26 up beats the fixed 0.55%. The mode
                     change is the edge; the digit is not.
      Stop_Min_Pts : floor in points = 3 x round-trip friction (2 x 5 + slip).
      Target_Room_Pct : target = entry + (box top - entry) x N%.
                     Measured from the ACTUAL fill, not the box bottom: a buy
                     stop below the market fills at the next bar's open, so
                     the fill sits inside the box at a median 0.40 of box
                     height - 37% of the range is gone before the trade starts.
                     DO NOT LOWER THIS. Sweep is monotone the other way:
                     35% room = -3,696 pts at 67.6% WR; 85% room = +2,572 at
                     51.9% WR. Only 24.3% of trades ever reach the box top,
                     and those 24.3% ARE the entire edge. Cutting the target
                     raises the win rate and destroys the expectancy.
                     2026-09-27 CORRECTION: the "9 of 9 plateau" was measured on
                     data that included 2026-06-17..09-24. On data up to 06-16
                     only, 85% LOSES to the swing target at 8 of 8 stop values
                     (-64 to -579 pts): the plateau was three live-window trades
                     (08-20, 08-31, 09-03). Not independently supported.
      Rule_On      : v18 turns the R1 consecutive-loss pause OFF. Streak_N=2
                     cost 1,038 net pts and moved max drawdown by 0
                     (-2,637 -> -2,637). It bought nothing. }
    Night_Only(false),
    Stop_Day_Pct(28),
    Stop_Min_Pts(60),
    Target_Room_Pct(85),

    Qual_New_On(false),         { v18: OFF. The box gate stays Min_Box_ATR 8.5 as in the live version;
                                  the RR x Risk_Pct gate belongs to the abandoned v16 design. }
    Stop_New_On(false),         { false = original ATR-buffer stop (live version) }
    Risk_Pct(0.5),              { per-trade risk, % of entry price. account 1.5% at 2 TMF lots }
    RR_Base(2.0),
    RR_Min(2.0),
    RR_Max(5.0),
    RR_Vol_Wks(4),              { recent window, weekly bars (Data4) }
    RR_Base_Wks(52),            { one-year baseline, weekly bars. 4 + 52 = 56 <= 99 }
    Box_Log_On(true),           { write one Print line per entry (Output window) }

    { --- R2b (2026-09-24): how "box wide enough" is measured ---
      1 = ATR multiple   : width >= Qual_ATR_Mult * ATR(15M)      (original, 8.5)
      2 = price percent  : width >= Qual_Pct * entry price / 100
      3 = cost multiple  : width >= Qual_Cost_Mult * round-trip cost in points
      4 = weekly range   : width >= Qual_Wk_Mult * average daily range of the
                           last Qual_Wk_Days sessions, AND
                           width >= Qual_Cost_Mult * Cost_Pts_RT
      Qual_Log_On prints EVERY box that forms, qualified or not, so the
      real distribution can be measured instead of assumed. }
    Qual_Mode(1),
    Qual_ATR_Mult(8.5),
    Qual_Pct(0.6),
    Qual_Cost_Mult(10),         { cost floor: box must cover N round trips }
    Cost_Pts_RT(10),            { round-trip friction in points per lot: 1000 NTD / 200 = 5 per side }
    Qual_Wk_Mult(0.4),          { box width >= N * weekly average daily range }
    Qual_Wk_Days(5),            { sessions used for the weekly average }
    Qual_Log_On(false),

    { --- V14 Matrix Dimensions --- }
    Entry_Zone_Pct(0.50),       { support zone = bottom 50% of box range (optimized from 0.30) }
    Min_Box_ATR(8.5),           { skip boxes smaller than N * 15M ATR (optimized from 3.0) }
    Swing_Lookback(80),         { 15M bars for dynamic swing high target (optimized from 32) }

    { --- Risk Management (15M) --- }
    ATR_Length(9),
    ATR_Stop_Mult(3.0),
    SL_Pct(0.55),               { V15: percentage stop cap. 0 = disabled. E.g. 0.55 = 0.55% of entry }
    Open_Block_End(945),        { V15: block entries filling before this MC time. 0 = disabled }
    Min_RR(1.0),                { V15: min reward/risk for entry. 0 = disabled. Optimizable }

    { --- Data3 (Daily) Filter Settings --- }
    Daily_MA_Fast(20),
    Daily_MA_Slow(60),

    { --- Holiday Flat Rule v3 (Iron Rule 2026-06-12) --- }
    Holiday_Flat_Time(415),
    Registry_Valid_Until(1270101),
    Manual_Kill_Switch(false),

    { --- Monthly Settlement Flat (2026-06-17) --- }
    Settlement_Flat_Time(1230),

    { --- Frozen SL (v13.2, always-on in v14) --- }
    Freeze_SL_On(true),

    { --- BE layer (DISABLED for range strategies, kept for compat) --- }
    BE_Trigger_Pts(0),
    BE_Offset_Pts(5),

    { --- v19 (2026-09-27): research switches, ALL OFF by default.
          With these defaults the file trades exactly like the live version. --- }
    Target_Mode(0),             { 0 = legacy: room% target when Stop_New_On, swing otherwise
                                  1 = swing high capped at box top (live version)
                                  2 = entry + (box top - entry) x Target_Room_Pct%
                                  Lets the stop and the target be tested one at a time. }
    Min_Gap_Hrs(0),             { no new entry within N calendar hours of the previous
                                  entry. 0 = off. Research only: passed 1 of 3 tests. }
    Size_Mode(0),               { 0 = fixed lots from the MC strategy properties (live)
                                  1 = lots = Acct_Capital x Risk_Acct_Pct% / risk per lot
                                  2 = same, on equity (Acct_Capital + NetProfit) }
    Acct_Capital(2000000),      { account size used by Size_Mode 1 and 2 }
    Risk_Acct_Pct(1.0),         { loss at the planned stop incl. round-trip cost, % of account }
    Max_Lots(2),                { hard cap on lots in Size_Mode 1 and 2 }

    { --- R1 loss rules (2026-09-23) --- }
    Rule_On(false), Rule_Lots(2), Daily_Cap_Pts(0), Weekly_Cap_Pts(0), Streak_N(2), Halt_DD_Pts(1500);

variables:
    { --- Data2 (60M) Box State --- }
    v_Ref_High(0),
    v_Ref_Low(0),
    v_Curr_Range(0),
    v_Ref_Range(0),
    v_is_in_consolidation(false),
    v_Box_Top(0),
    v_Box_Btm(0),

    { --- V14 Matrix State --- }
    v_Mid_Line(0),
    v_Box_Range(0),
    v_Box_Qualified(false),

    { --- R2 box state --- }
    v_Top_New(0), v_Btm_New(0), v_Hi2(0), v_Lo2(0),
    v_HiCnt(0), v_LoCnt(0), v_Touch_Tol(0), v_Drift(0),
    v_Win_Hi(0), v_Win_Lo(0), v_Win_Rng(0), v_Consol_New(false),
    v_Box_Age(0), v_i(0), v_hb(0), v_lb(0),
    v_Stop_Px(0), v_Stop_Dist(0), v_Plan_RR(0), v_Entry_Px(0),
    v_Qual_Need(0), v_Box_Pct(0), v_Box_ATRx(0), v_Box_Costx(0), v_Prev_BoxTop(0), v_Qual_Flag(0),
    v_Wk_Rng(0), v_Box_Wkx(0), v_Qual_Need2(0), v_Pass1(false), v_Pass2(false),
    v_RR(2), v_Need_W(0), v_Target_Px(0),
    v_PrevDayRngPct(0), v_Day_Block(false), v_Stop_Floor(0), v_SumR(0),
    v_Wk_Now(0), v_Wk_Base(0),
    v_Support_Zone(0),
    v_Swing_High(0),

    { --- Data2 Trend Filter --- }
    v_60M_MA(0),
    v_Trend_Dir(0),

    { --- Data3 Daily Filter --- }
    v_Daily_MA_Fast(0),
    v_Daily_MA_Slow(0),
    v_Daily_Filter(false),

    { --- Data1 (15M) Execution --- }
    v_Current_ATR(0),
    v_ATR_Buffer(0),
    v_SL_Distance(0),          { V15: SetStopLoss distance (engine level) }
    v_Opening_Block(false),    { V15: true during day-session opening no-trade window }
    v_RR_Qualified(true),      { V15: true when box R:R meets Min_RR threshold }

    { --- Holiday / Settlement --- }
    v_Holiday_Block(false),
    v_Registry_Expired(false),
    Registry_Warn_ID(-1),
    hidx(0),
    v_Settlement_Day(false),

    { --- Frozen SL / Target --- }
    v_SL_Locked(false),
    v_Frozen_SL(0),
    v_Frozen_Target(0),
    v_Work_SL(0),
    v_Work_Target(0),
    v_SL_Pct_Floor(0),        { V15: percentage leg SL price }
    v_BE_Armed(false),
    v_BE_IsFloor(false),
    v_Tgt_Room(false), v_Now_Min(0), v_Last_Entry_Min(-99999999), v_Entry_Cnt(0), v_Prev_Entry_Cnt(0),
    v_Gap_Block(false), v_Lots(1), v_Plan_Stop_Pts(0), v_Risk_Per_Lot(0), v_Risk_Budget(0),
    { R1 loss rules } v_Rule_Allow(true), v_Skip_Next(false), v_R_LastDate(0), v_R_DayNP(0), v_R_WeekNP(0), v_R_LastTT(0), v_R_LastNP(0), v_R_Streak(0), v_R_Peak(0), v_R_Unit(1), v_R_Halt_Done(false), v_R_Shadow(0);

arrays:
    Holiday_Tail[80](0);
{ ==========================================================
  LOSS RULES R1 (2026-09-23): daily/weekly loss cap, streak pause,
  drawdown halt. Amounts are POINTS per Rule_Lots contracts, so the
  same inputs work on TXF (200/pt) and TMF (10/pt).
  Rule_On = false must reproduce the pre-R1 strategy exactly.
  ========================================================== }
if Date <> v_R_LastDate then begin
    if v_R_LastDate = 0 then
        v_R_WeekNP = NetProfit
    else if DayOfWeek(Date) < DayOfWeek(v_R_LastDate) or DateToJulian(Date) - DateToJulian(v_R_LastDate) >= 7 then
        v_R_WeekNP = NetProfit;
    v_R_DayNP = NetProfit;
    v_R_LastDate = Date;
end;
v_R_Unit = BigPointValue * Rule_Lots;
if TotalTrades > v_R_LastTT then begin
    if NetProfit - v_R_LastNP < 0 then
        v_R_Streak = v_R_Streak + 1
    else
        v_R_Streak = 0;
    if Streak_N > 0 and v_R_Streak >= Streak_N then begin
        v_Skip_Next = true;
        v_R_Streak = 0;
    end;
    v_R_LastNP = NetProfit;
    v_R_LastTT = TotalTrades;
end;
{ --- drawdown halt (2026-09-24: one-trade pause, not a permanent lock) ---
  When the drawdown from the equity peak exceeds Halt_DD_Pts the NEXT entry is
  skipped once, then trading resumes and the peak is reset to the current
  equity so the same drawdown cannot fire again and again. A permanent lock
  cannot be released inside a backtest, which is why the earlier version
  stopped trading for good in 2024. }
if NetProfit > v_R_Peak then v_R_Peak = NetProfit;
if Halt_DD_Pts > 0 and v_R_Unit > 0 and v_R_Halt_Done = false then begin
    if (v_R_Peak - NetProfit) / v_R_Unit > Halt_DD_Pts then begin
        v_Skip_Next   = true;
        v_R_Halt_Done = true;
        v_R_Peak      = NetProfit;
    end;
end;
{ re-arm once a new equity high is made }
if v_R_Halt_Done and NetProfit >= v_R_Peak then v_R_Halt_Done = false;
if v_R_Shadow > 0 then begin
    if High >= v_R_Shadow then v_Skip_Next = false;
    v_R_Shadow = 0;
end;
v_Rule_Allow = true;
if Rule_On = false then
    v_Skip_Next = false
else begin
    if v_R_Unit > 0 then begin
        if Daily_Cap_Pts > 0 and (NetProfit - v_R_DayNP) / v_R_Unit <= -Daily_Cap_Pts then v_Rule_Allow = false;
        if Weekly_Cap_Pts > 0 and (NetProfit - v_R_WeekNP) / v_R_Unit <= -Weekly_Cap_Pts then v_Rule_Allow = false;
    end;

end;


{ ==========================================
  0. Holiday Tail Registry (TAIFEX-verified, shared with L1/L2)
  ========================================== }

if CurrentBar = 1 then begin
    Holiday_Tail[1]  = 1190913;  Holiday_Tail[2]  = 1191010;
    Holiday_Tail[3]  = 1200101;
    { 2020 } Holiday_Tail[4]  = 1200121;  Holiday_Tail[5]  = 1200228;
